{
  "_comment": "Sprite sheets are authored at art_scale x logical size. frames run horizontally from `col` on `row`. Sprite keys match tower/enemy keys exactly so nothing has to be remapped at runtime.",
  "_decor_note": "Floor markings: invented parody brand squares. Placed deterministically per map on plain buildable tiles only, and drawn in a very dark band so they never compete with gameplay. Not real trademarks. Any key starting with `_` inside `sheets` is ignored by the sheet builder.",

  "_resolution_note": "art_scale multiplies every sheet's frame size at generation time; the UV maths does not care, so raising it costs only canvas memory. 3 puts a 64-unit logical sprite on a 192px frame, which stays sharp well past the deepest zoom.",
  "pixel_art": false,
  "art_scale": 3,

  "_fx_note": "The `muzzle`, `smoke`, `spark` and `dust` sheets are the ambient half of the art. They are emitted by the renderer's particle pool, not by the simulation, so they never consume the gameplay effect budget.",

  "sheets": {
